      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2)(1)+(0)(1)+(1)(1)+(2)(1)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{6})≈{33.56}^{∘}.\n$$",
